 **Edge Cases and Pitfalls**
-*   **Pointer Shifting:** Loading a model into the octree can destroy the model's internal octree structure by shifting all pointers relative to the main octree's size. This is noted as a temporary solution in the source [S1, unofficial].
-*   **Boundary Conditions:** The algorithm assumes coordinates are within the initial bounding box defined by the root. Growth handles missing nodes, but out-of-bounds coordinates may require external clamping or tree expansion logic not detailed in this specific method [G].
-*   **Precision:** Floating-point comparisons (`x > mid[0]`) are used. For very high detail levels, precision errors may affect octant determination [G].
