 ## Background
-This method originates from the `voxl` project, an open-source voxel renderer [S1, unofficial]. It represents a basic implementation of dynamic sparse voxel octree construction, focusing on the core mechanics of node insertion and parent finding without advanced optimizations like Morton codes or out-of-core storage. The code is part of a larger system that includes camera management and frame rendering.
